From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:02:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] browse: panorama pages read cover sizes before they are shown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Masonry places each cover at its final ratio, so the height/width has to
be known before the page is returned. After an HttpSource page loads, and
only while the catalogue mode is ComfortableGrid or CompactGrid panorama,
each unknown cover is probed with the source OkHttp client and headers
(Referer included). The request is Range bytes=0-32767, at most 32 KB is
read, and a 200 that ignored Range is cancelled instead of drained. JPEG
is walked by segment length so an APP1 EXIF thumbnail is not the size;
if those lengths put SOF past the first window, one follow-up reads up to
128 KB. Six probes run at a time. The first page (refresh) waits for them inside a
400 ms budget; appended pages are returned at once and probed in the
background (2 s budget, cancelled when the source is invalidated), since
they land below the viewport and a learnt shape only relayouts that tail.
Ratios are stored as they finish. Ids already in PanoramaCoverShapes are skipped.
Local sources are not probed. A cover that does not finish, or whose
format is unknown, stays on the placeholder.

